From 2d18260862cb8652fd34a2a8e667fa3c017404f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Serhii Nikolaichuk <nikolaichuk.s.f@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 13:15:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] sevsnp: verify VCEK and VLEK chains up to AMD's roots
 (go-sev-guest v0.15.0)

go-sev-guest v0.15.0 no longer takes the ASK or ASVK from the evidence's
certificate chain: with no TrustedRoots it checks the chain only against its
embedded defaults, which hold the ASK and ARK of each product line but no
ASVK. Every VLEK report, as AWS hosts issue, then fails with "root of trust
missing intermediate certificate authority certificate for key VLEK".

Pass TrustedRoots built from the six chains go-sev-guest embeds (VCEK and
VLEK for Milan, Genoa and Turin), the same chains AMD's KDS serves. The
Turin VLEK chain ends with a blank line that kds.ParseProductCertChain
refuses (google/go-sev-guest#206), so it is trimmed first.

The new test runs a real VLEK report from an AWS EC2 c6a.large guest: it
fails on v0.15.0 without TrustedRoots, passes on v0.14.2-pre and with this
change, and a report with one bit changed is still refused on its signature.
